o I'm headed out of there and I  see this door partially open at the end  of one of the halls and this older woman  standing in the dark so I think oh she  must be getting ready to go out and  leave her room well turns out I was  right  in a way once I get closer she walks out  of the room and she's standing in the  hall right it seems like she's looking  at me but when I saw her eyes it was  more like she was listening with past me  or looking through me at something like  her head was pointed in my direction but  it's almost like she didn't see me at  all she was in her own world and in this  world of hers there was a ghost standing  just past where I was I know it's hard  to picture but that's the best way I can  really describe it so that was  unsettling but not as unsettling as what  would come next the voice it was like  something out of a horror movie and what  she said didn't make it any better  now I don't remember her exact words so  I'm just paraphrasing but it was  something along the lines of why hello  Gerald why don't you come in and have  some supper make you some supper and  then she actually started laughing and  meanwhile I just didn't even think about  responding to any other I just kept  walking and never looked back she kept  talking as I walked away but I didn't  hear so yeah that was one of the  creepier things I'd ever seen but I  guess it could have been like a prank or  something or maybe she had a bluetooth  on but I didn't see maybe I was honestly  just trying to come up with an excuse  for my own comfort at that point but  after that I went out got some food and  came back and at that point I had pretty  much forgotten about it all but then I  turned into that hallway again and what  do I see in the same exact spot where  the woman had wandered out before there  was a police officer taking down some  notes and the door that the woman came  out of was open and the place was  cleared out I never found out what  happened that night while I was getting  food but I still do wonder if I had just  been lucky to have not been a victim  clearly something went down while I was  gone and it was big enough to get the  cops called and start an investigation  what stuck with me more than anything  was the look in that woman's eye she  just looked so Hollow after thinking  more about the situation I came up with  the theory that she was having some kind  of flashback in her head possibly a  trauma induced reaction what led me to  this theory well first I want to analyze  why she was even staying at this hotel  this isn't in like a touristy part of LA  it's at least thirty minutes away from  the beach 30 minutes away from Universal  and 45 minutes away from Hollywood so  that left me with  possibility she's visiting family or  there's something wrong at home causing  her to have to stay in the hotel the  same reason that I was technically  staying there based on her behavior I've  decided to explore the ladder as that  seems more likely to me we have very  little to go off of in the situation  really just what she said which  unfortunately I don't remember it  perfectly word for word this was before  I started doing true fear so I didn't  think to write it down or anything but I  think her dialogue does offer some  possible clues as to what was going on  so first there's this character Gerald  who she seemed to be talking to based on  the way that she was talking to him and  the fact that she asked him to come in  for supper Gerald may have been her  husband or possibly her son at the  beginning of the interaction she seemed  kind of surprised to see Gerald so I  took this as they had been apart for  some time and maybe she was daydreaming  or hallucinating about seeing him again  that's why I think this may have been  trauma related in some way for example  if Gerald was her husband I get the  sense that he hurt her and abandoned her  in some way causing her to fall into a  deep depression and replayed the idea 